If you are handling the transition for the {{employees}} people leaving {{company}}, I have a paragraph for the separation notes. {{line_timing}}

It points people to NextChapter, the world's first job transition platform: career pivots, learning and retraining, networking support, and exclusive jobs and recruiters. {{line_open_roles}} People opt in, and you share no names. {{line_board}}

I can send the paragraph and link today. Who on your team should receive it?

{{first_name}},

Quick question: who owns the transition for the {{employees}} people leaving {{company}}? {{line_open_roles}}

I run NextChapter, the world's first job transition platform: career pivots, retraining, networking support, and exclusive jobs and recruiters. The older tools are dated and people do not like them. You may know the right person better than any directory does. If you can point me to them, I'll take it from there and keep it to one short note.

{{first_name}},

{{line_local}} {{line_company}} {{line_timing}}

I built a working demo of NextChapter for {{board}}'s region from those public notices, so you can see what your professional job seekers would get: local jobs first, a skills-gap plan, AI training, and an account free to them. {{line_open_roles}}

I would like to run a pilot with one shared measure: how many referred people joined and, among those who choose to share it, how many are interviewing at 45 days. Want the demo link?
